{"id": "tea:yogataravali:2", "source": "src:yogataravali", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "Sadāśiva taught a hundred and twenty-five thousand methods of laya; we hold the samādhi of attention to the inner sound (nādānusandhāna) to be the most honoured of the layas.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Verse number recalled with moderate confidence; parallel to HYP 4.66 (which says 'a crore and a quarter' and ascribes them to Ādinātha).", "practices": ["prc:nadanusandhana"], "concepts": ["cpt:laya-natha", "cpt:nada"], "cross_refs": ["tea:hatha-yoga-pradipika:4.65-66"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogataravali:topic.amanaska", "source": "src:yogataravali", "location": {"ref": "topic.amanaska"}, "paraphrase": "With the breath stilled and the mind dissolved the yogin reaches the mindless state (amanaska), the natural state (sahaja) — rājayoga — in which he is liberated while living.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:taraka-amanaska", "cpt:sahaja", "cpt:jivanmukti"], "terms": ["trm:amanaska", "trm:sahaja"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogataravali:topic.bandhas-kevala", "source": "src:yogataravali", "location": {"ref": "topic.bandhas-kevala"}, "paraphrase": "The three locks applied together lead to spontaneous retention (kevala kumbhaka), in which the breath stops of itself without inhalation or exhalation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "practices": ["prc:mula-bandha", "prc:uddiyana-bandha", "prc:jalandhara-bandha", "prc:kevala-kumbhaka"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
